# The fixture server's policy: public-key authentication with the key the fixture
# generated, nothing else.
#
# Password and keyboard-interactive authentication are off because the product's supported
# credential path is the user's existing key or agent, and a fixture that accepted a
# password would let a real regression in that path look like a pass. Forwarding and
# tunnels are off because no read uses them; the client disables them as well, and the
# server refusing them is the second half of that guarantee.
Port 22
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0

HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key
HostKeyAlgorithms ssh-ed25519

PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PermitRootLogin no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
AllowUsers gituser

AllowAgentForwarding no
AllowTcpForwarding no
PermitTunnel no
X11Forwarding no
PermitUserEnvironment no

PrintMotd no
LogLevel VERBOSE
PidFile /run/sshd.pid
AcceptEnv LANG LC_*
